Look at Xanthian's post elsewhere in this thread- he thinks there
should be no altar creation at all, but I would use his arguments to
say that there should be *almost* no altar creation at all. After all,
nethack is a game of options, so imnsho anything that adds more options
to the game is good. Wherever there's a risk of altering game balance,
however, those options should be made so insanely rare/ dangerous/
difficult/ obscure that they would only occur one game in every
thousand, leaving the vast majority of games unnaffected.

Look at the wand of wishing- if it had a one in five chance of being
generated on Dlvl1, people would rightly say that is unbalanced the
game and made ascension too easy. That's not to say the WoW should be
removed from the game entirely though, or even from Dlvl1 entirely. An
early WoW is still possible, just very very unlikely. This rarity
preserves game balance. In fact, a wand of wishing is actually
guaranteed later on but it doesn't unbalance the game because by that
point the character should be fairly powerful anyway.

Similarly, we could use rarity to preserve game balance in the case of
altar creation: IMHO it should be  so ridiculously difficult and
dangerous to create an altar that only a powerful and/or lucky
character would stand a chance of pulling it off. If anything, altar
creation as I suggested it would reduce the number of ascensions,
because so many additional players would die in the attempt- and that's
a good thing, imo.
If the difficulties in altar creation turn out to be excessive, they
can always be toned down in later releases when the devteam can draw on
the playtesting experiences of the community and balance it properly.

